From: nuubOS Project <noreply@nuubos.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] nuubOS: 400x300 and 480x360 GLideN64 resolutions

The 4:3 resolution option jumps from native 320x240 to 640x480, four
times the pixels: on the H700 (Mali-G31 MP1) that halves the frame rate.
1.25x and 1.5x let a game render sharper while keeping full speed; the
core already parses any WxH.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [nuubOS specific]
---
--- a/libretro/libretro_core_options.h
+++ b/libretro/libretro_core_options.h
@@ -92,6 +92,8 @@
         "gliden64",
         {
             {"320x240", NULL},
+            {"400x300", NULL},
+            {"480x360", NULL},
             {"640x480", NULL},
             {"960x720", NULL},
             {"1280x960", NULL},
